@startuml
title Gym pushup-counter: a complete session

actor User
participant "PushupCounter\n(widget)" as Widget
participant "PushupRepCounter" as RepCounter
participant "MediaPipePoseSource" as Pose
participant "Camera (device)" as Camera
participant "apps/web\nLogWorkoutScreen" as Host
participant "LoggingApiClient" as Logging
participant "services/logging" as Server

User -> Widget: click Start
Widget -> Pose: start(listener)
Pose -> Camera: getUserMedia(video)
Camera --> Pose: MediaStream
loop every animation frame
  Camera --> Pose: VideoFrame
  Pose -> Widget: listener(landmarks)
  Widget -> RepCounter: processFrame(landmarks)
  RepCounter --> Widget: count updated
end
User -> Widget: click Finish
Widget -> Pose: stop()
Pose -> Camera: release tracks
Widget --> Host: onComplete(count)
Host -> Logging: logWorkout({ kind: "pushup", reps: count }, token, idempotencyKey)
Logging -> Server: POST /workouts (Idempotency-Key)
Server --> Logging: 201 { workout }
Logging --> Host: LogWorkoutResponse

note over Widget, Camera
  Camera frames and MediaPipe inference
  stay on the device. Only the final count
  is sent over the network.
end note

@enduml
